IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc12-logic`

-- ccc12-part9-resembling-theft.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part IX, "Offences Resembling Theft": sections 335 to 342.2.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc12-part9-theft.l4 and NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc12)").
-- Answers taken from another provision are INPUTS named for that provision (`s 2 <term>: ...`, `s 322 ...`, `s 320.11 ...`, `s 787(1) ...`); never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Offences Resembling Theft (ss 335 to 342.2)`

§§ `Section 335 -- taking a motor vehicle or vessel without consent`

-- (1) is "subject to subsection (1.1)", so the exception is called inside the offence function: an occupant who attempted to leave, or left, is outside the offence.
-- src:6635 | Taking motor vehicle or vessel or found therein without consent
-- src:6636 | 335 (1) Subject to subsection (1.1), every one who, without the consent of the owner, takes a motor vehicle or vessel with intent to drive, use, navigate or operate it or cause it to be driven, used, navigated or operated, or is an occupant of a motor vehicle or vessel knowing that it was taken without the consent of the owner, is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 335(1) (src:6635-6636)
GIVEN `the thing is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a vessel, by s 335(2) the thing is a vessel for the purposes of subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person acted without the consent of the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person takes it with intent to drive, use, navigate or operate it or cause it to be driven, used, navigated or operated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an occupant of it knowing that it was taken without the consent of the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on becoming aware that it was taken without the consent of the owner, the occupant attempted to leave it, to the extent that it was feasible to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on becoming aware that it was taken without the consent of the owner, the occupant actually left it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 335(1) the person is guilty of the offence of taking a motor vehicle or vessel without consent, or of being an occupant of one taken without consent` MEANS
    `ccc12 and` (`ccc12 or` `the thing is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` `the thing is a vessel, by s 335(2) the thing is a vessel for the purposes of subsection (1)`)
                (JUST (`the taking limb` OR `the occupant limb`))
    -- JUST FALSE where neither limb holds, or the thing is a definite no to both: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every one who, without the consent of the owner, takes a motor vehicle or vessel with intent to drive, use, navigate or operate it or cause it to be driven, used, navigated or operated, or is an occupant of a motor vehicle or vessel knowing that it was taken without the consent of the owner"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 2 "motor vehicle" or the s 320.11 "vessel" answer was not given
    WHERE
        `the taking limb` MEANS `the person acted without the consent of the owner` AND `the person takes it with intent to drive, use, navigate or operate it or cause it to be driven, used, navigated or operated`
        `the occupant limb` MEANS
                `the person is an occupant of it knowing that it was taken without the consent of the owner`
            AND NOT (`s 335(1.1) subsection (1) applies to an occupant` `the person is an occupant of it knowing that it was taken without the consent of the owner` `on becoming aware that it was taken without the consent of the owner, the occupant attempted to leave it, to the extent that it was feasible to do so` `on becoming aware that it was taken without the consent of the owner, the occupant actually left it` EQUALS JUST FALSE)   -- "Subject to subsection (1.1)"

@ref Criminal Code s 335(1) (src:6636-6636)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 335(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- "is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction": one limb, the summary one

-- src:6637 | Exception
-- src:6638 | (1.1) Subsection (1) does not apply to an occupant of a motor vehicle or vessel who, on becoming aware that it was taken without the consent of the owner, attempted to leave the motor vehicle or vessel, to the extent that it was feasible to do so, or actually left the motor vehicle or vessel.
@ref Criminal Code s 335(1.1) (src:6637-6638)
GIVEN `the person is an occupant of a motor vehicle or vessel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on becoming aware that it was taken without the consent of the owner, the occupant attempted to leave it, to the extent that it was feasible to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on becoming aware that it was taken without the consent of the owner, the occupant actually left it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 335(1.1) subsection (1) applies to an occupant` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an occupant of a motor vehicle or vessel`
      AND (   `on becoming aware that it was taken without the consent of the owner, the occupant attempted to leave it, to the extent that it was feasible to do so`
           OR `on becoming aware that it was taken without the consent of the owner, the occupant actually left it`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to an occupant of a motor vehicle or vessel who, on becoming aware that it was taken without the consent of the owner, attempted to leave the motor vehicle or vessel, to the extent that it was feasible to do so, or actually left the motor vehicle or vessel"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says no only for an occupant who attempted to leave or left; for anyone else it says nothing

-- src:6639 | Definition of vessel
-- src:6640 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), vessel has the same meaning as in section 320.11.
@ref Criminal Code s 335(2) (src:6639-6640)
GIVEN `the thing is a vessel, by s 320.11 the thing is a vessel` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 335(2) the thing is a vessel for the purposes of subsection (1)` MEANS
    `the thing is a vessel, by s 320.11 the thing is a vessel`   -- "vessel has the same meaning as in section 320.11": the answer of section 320.11 (another part) is taken as an input; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where it was not given

§§ `Sections 336 to 341 -- breach of trust, cattle, drift timber, documents, concealment`

-- src:6641 | Criminal breach of trust
-- src:6642 | 336 Every one who, being a trustee of anything for the use or benefit, whether in whole or in part, of another person, or for a public or charitable purpose, converts, with intent to defraud and in contravention of his trust, that thing or any part of it to a use that is not authorized by the trust is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 336 (src:6641-6642)
GIVEN `the person is a trustee, by s 2 trustee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is held for the use or benefit, whether in whole or in part, of another person, or for a public or charitable purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person converted that thing or any part of it to a use that is not authorized by the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person did so with intent to defraud and in contravention of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 336 the person commits criminal breach of trust` MEANS
    IF    `the thing is held for the use or benefit, whether in whole or in part, of another person, or for a public or charitable purpose`
      AND `the person converted that thing or any part of it to a use that is not authorized by the trust`
      AND `the person did so with intent to defraud and in contravention of the trust`
    THEN `the person is a trustee, by s 2 trustee`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 2 "trustee" answer was not given; JUST FALSE where it is a definite no
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who, being a trustee of anything for the use or benefit, whether in whole or in part, of another person, or for a public or charitable purpose, converts, with intent to defraud and in contravention of his trust, that thing or any part of it to a use that is not authorized by the trust"

@ref Criminal Code s 336 (src:6642-6642)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 336 the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`)

-- src:6643 | 337 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 33]
@ref Criminal Code s 337 (src:6643)
`s 337 as the text shows it` MEANS "337 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 33]"

-- src:6644 | Fraudulently taking cattle or defacing brand
-- src:6645 | 338 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, without the consent of the owner,
-- src:6646 | (a) fraudulently takes, holds, keeps in his possession, conceals, receives, appropriates, purchases or sells cattle that are found astray, or
-- src:6647 | (b) fraudulently, in whole or in part,
-- src:6648 | (i) obliterates, alters or defaces a brand or mark on cattle, or
-- src:6649 | (ii) makes a false or counterfeit brand or mark on cattle.
@ref Criminal Code s 338(1) (src:6644-6649)
GIVEN `the animals are cattle, by s 2 cattle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person acted without the consent of the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cattle are found astray` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently takes, holds, keeps in their possession, conceals, receives, appropriates, purchases or sells them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently, in whole or in part, obliterates, alters or defaces a brand or mark on cattle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently, in whole or in part, makes a false or counterfeit brand or mark on cattle` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338(1) the person is guilty of fraudulently taking cattle or defacing a brand` MEANS
    IF `the person acted without the consent of the owner`
    THEN `ccc12 and` `the animals are cattle, by s 2 cattle`
                     (JUST (    (`the cattle are found astray` AND `the person fraudulently takes, holds, keeps in their possession, conceals, receives, appropriates, purchases or sells them`)
                            OR `the person fraudulently, in whole or in part, obliterates, alters or defaces a brand or mark on cattle`
                            OR `the person fraudulently, in whole or in part, makes a false or counterfeit brand or mark on cattle`))
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 2 "cattle" answer was not given
         -- JUST FALSE where no paragraph holds or the animals are a definite no: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence ... who, without the consent of the owner, (a) fraudulently takes, holds, keeps in his possession, conceals, receives, appropriates, purchases or sells cattle that are found astray"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who, without the consent of the owner"

@ref Criminal Code s 338(1) (src:6645-6645)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 338(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`)   -- indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than five years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- or guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction

-- src:6650 | Punishment for theft of cattle
-- src:6651 | (2) Every person who commits theft of cattle is guilty of
-- src:6652 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:6653 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 338(2) (src:6650-6653)
GIVEN `the person commits theft, by s 322 the person commits theft` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the property is cattle, by s 2 cattle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338(2) the person commits theft of cattle` MEANS
    `ccc12 and` `the person commits theft, by s 322 the person commits theft` `the property is cattle, by s 2 cattle`
    -- JUST FALSE where either is a definite no: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who commits theft of cattle"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 322 or the s 2 "cattle" answer was not given

@ref Criminal Code s 338(2) (src:6651-6653)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 338(2) the punishment for theft of cattle` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (a) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction

-- src:6654 | Evidence of property in cattle
-- src:6655 | (3) In any proceedings under this Act, evidence that cattle are marked with a brand or mark that is recorded or registered in accordance with any Act is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that the cattle are owned by the registered owner of that brand or mark.
@ref Criminal Code s 338(3) (src:6654-6655)
GIVEN `the cattle are marked with a brand or mark that is recorded or registered in accordance with any Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338(3) the evidence is proof that the cattle are owned by the registered owner of the brand or mark` MEANS
    IF `the cattle are marked with a brand or mark that is recorded or registered in accordance with any Act`
    THEN IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that the cattle are owned by the registered owner of that brand or mark"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of cattle marked with a recorded or registered brand or mark

-- (4): the burden is on the accused "if the accused is not the registered owner ..., unless it appears that possession ... was without the knowledge and authority, sanction or approval of the accused" (fork F-UNLESS).
-- src:6656 | Presumption from possession
-- src:6657 | (4) Where an accused is charged with an offence under subsection (1) or (2), the burden of proving that the cattle came lawfully into the possession of the accused or his employee or into the possession of another person on behalf of the accused is on the accused, if the accused is not the registered owner of the brand or mark with which the cattle are marked, unless it appears that possession of the cattle by an employee of the accused or by another person on behalf of the accused was without the knowledge and authority, sanction or approval of the accused.
@ref Criminal Code s 338(4) (src:6656-6657)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with an offence under subsection 338(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is the registered owner of the brand or mark with which the cattle are marked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears that possession of the cattle by an employee of the accused or by another person on behalf of the accused was without the knowledge and authority, sanction or approval of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338(4) the burden of proving that the cattle came lawfully into possession is on the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is charged with an offence under subsection 338(1) or (2)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is charged with an offence under subsection (1) or (2)"
        IF `the accused is the registered owner of the brand or mark with which the cattle are marked`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the accused is not the registered owner of the brand or mark with which the cattle are marked"
        IF `it appears that possession of the cattle by an employee of the accused or by another person on behalf of the accused was without the knowledge and authority, sanction or approval of the accused`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it appears that possession of the cattle by an employee of the accused or by another person on behalf of the accused was without the knowledge and authority, sanction or approval of the accused"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:6658 | Taking possession, etc., of drift timber
-- src:6659 | 339 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, without the consent of the owner,
-- src:6660 | (a) fraudulently takes, holds, keeps in their possession, conceals, receives, appropriates, purchases or sells any lumber or lumbering equipment that is found adrift, cast ashore or lying on or embedded in the bed or bottom, or on the bank or beach, of a river, stream or lake in Canada, or in the harbours or any of the coastal waters of Canada;
-- src:6661 | (b) removes, alters, obliterates or defaces a mark or number on such lumber or lumbering equipment; or
-- src:6662 | (c) refuses to deliver such lumber or lumbering equipment up to the owner or to the person in charge of it on behalf of the owner or to a person authorized by the owner to receive it.
@ref Criminal Code s 339(1) (src:6658-6662)
GIVEN `the person acted without the consent of the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is lumber, by s 339(6) lumber` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is lumbering equipment, by s 339(6) lumbering equipment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is found adrift, cast ashore or lying on or embedded in the bed or bottom, or on the bank or beach, of a river, stream or lake in Canada, or in the harbours or any of the coastal waters of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently takes, holds, keeps in their possession, conceals, receives, appropriates, purchases or sells it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person removes, alters, obliterates or defaces a mark or number on it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person refuses to deliver it up to the owner or to the person in charge of it on behalf of the owner or to a person authorized by the owner to receive it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339(1) the person is guilty of the offence of taking possession of drift timber` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted without the consent of the owner`
      AND `the thing is found adrift, cast ashore or lying on or embedded in the bed or bottom, or on the bank or beach, of a river, stream or lake in Canada, or in the harbours or any of the coastal waters of Canada`
      AND (   `the person fraudulently takes, holds, keeps in their possession, conceals, receives, appropriates, purchases or sells it`
           OR `the person removes, alters, obliterates or defaces a mark or number on it`
           OR `the person refuses to deliver it up to the owner or to the person in charge of it on behalf of the owner or to a person authorized by the owner to receive it`)
    THEN `ccc12 or` `the thing is lumber, by s 339(6) lumber` `the thing is lumbering equipment, by s 339(6) lumbering equipment`
         -- JUST FALSE where both are definite no's; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where an answer of subsection (6) was not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence ... who, without the consent of the owner, (a) fraudulently takes, holds, keeps in their possession, conceals, receives, appropriates, purchases or sells any lumber or lumbering equipment that is found adrift"

@ref Criminal Code s 339(1) (src:6659-6659)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 339(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`)
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:6663 | Dealer in second-hand goods
-- src:6664 | (2) Every one who, being a dealer in second-hand goods of any kind, trades or traffics in or has in his possession for sale or traffic any lumbering equipment that is marked with the mark, brand, registered timber mark, name or initials of a person, without the written consent of that person, is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 339(2) (src:6663-6664)
GIVEN `the person is a dealer in second-hand goods of any kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person trades or traffics in or has in their possession for sale or traffic the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is lumbering equipment, by s 339(6) lumbering equipment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is marked with the mark, brand, registered timber mark, name or initials of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted without the written consent of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339(2) the dealer in second-hand goods is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a dealer in second-hand goods of any kind`
      AND `the person trades or traffics in or has in their possession for sale or traffic the thing`
      AND `it is marked with the mark, brand, registered timber mark, name or initials of a person`
      AND `the person acted without the written consent of that person`
    THEN `the thing is lumbering equipment, by s 339(6) lumbering equipment`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the answer of subsection (6) was not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who, being a dealer in second-hand goods of any kind, trades or traffics in or has in his possession for sale or traffic any lumbering equipment that is marked with the mark, brand, registered timber mark, name or initials of a person, without the written consent of that person"

@ref Criminal Code s 339(2) (src:6664-6664)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 339(2) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- "is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction"

-- src:6665 | Search for timber unlawfully detained
-- src:6666 | (3) A peace officer who suspects, on reasonable grounds, that any lumber owned by any person and bearing the registered timber mark of that person is kept or detained in or on any place without the knowledge or consent of that person, may enter into or on that place to ascertain whether or not it is detained there without the knowledge or consent of that person.
@ref Criminal Code s 339(3) (src:6665-6666)
GIVEN `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer suspects, on reasonable grounds, that any lumber owned by any person and bearing the registered timber mark of that person is kept or detained in or on the place without the knowledge or consent of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339(3) the peace officer may enter into or on the place to ascertain whether the lumber is detained there` MEANS
    IF `the officer suspects, on reasonable grounds, that any lumber owned by any person and bearing the registered timber mark of that person is kept or detained in or on the place without the knowledge or consent of that person`
    THEN CONSIDER `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("may enter") granted to "a peace officer who suspects"; for a person who is not a peace officer the subsection grants nothing and denies nothing (a grant, not a bar)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the s 2 "peace officer" answer was not given
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("may enter") granted to a peace officer who suspects on reasonable grounds; outside that limit the subsection grants nothing and denies nothing

-- src:6667 | Evidence of property in timber
-- src:6668 | (4) Where any lumber or lumbering equipment is marked with a timber mark or a boom chain brand registered under any Act, the mark or brand is, in proceedings under subsection (1), and, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that it is the property of the registered owner of the mark or brand.
@ref Criminal Code s 339(4) (src:6667-6668)
GIVEN `the lumber or lumbering equipment is marked with a timber mark or a boom chain brand registered under any Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are proceedings under subsection 339(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339(4) the mark or brand is proof that the lumber or lumbering equipment is the property of the registered owner` MEANS
    IF `the lumber or lumbering equipment is marked with a timber mark or a boom chain brand registered under any Act` AND `the proceedings are proceedings under subsection 339(1)`
    THEN IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that it is the property of the registered owner of the mark or brand"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of marked lumber or equipment "in proceedings under subsection (1)"

-- src:6669 | Presumption from possession
-- src:6670 | (5) Where an accused or his servants or agents are in possession of lumber or lumbering equipment marked with the mark, brand, registered timber mark, name or initials of another person, the burden of proving that it came lawfully into his possession or into possession of his servants or agents is, in proceedings under subsection (1), on the accused.
@ref Criminal Code s 339(5) (src:6669-6670)
GIVEN `the accused or the accused's servants or agents are in possession of lumber or lumbering equipment marked with the mark, brand, registered timber mark, name or initials of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are proceedings under subsection 339(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339(5) the burden of proving that the lumber or lumbering equipment came lawfully into possession is on the accused` MEANS
    IF    `the accused or the accused's servants or agents are in possession of lumber or lumbering equipment marked with the mark, brand, registered timber mark, name or initials of another person`
      AND `the proceedings are proceedings under subsection 339(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused or his servants or agents are in possession of lumber or lumbering equipment marked with the mark, brand, registered timber mark, name or initials of another person, the burden of proving that it came lawfully into his possession or into possession of his servants or agents is, in proceedings under subsection (1), on the accused" (a "Where" gate unmet: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- (6): "coastal waters of Canada includes ..."; "lumber means ..."; "lumbering equipment includes ...".
DECLARE `s 339(6) waters` IS ONE OF
    `s 339(6) all of Queen Charlotte Sound`
    `s 339(6) all the Strait of Georgia`
    `s 339(6) the Canadian waters of the Strait of Juan de Fuca`
    `s 339(6) other waters`

-- src:6673 | coastal waters of Canada includes all of Queen Charlotte Sound, all the Strait of Georgia and the Canadian waters of the Strait of Juan de Fuca; (eaux côtières du Canada)
@ref Criminal Code s 339(6) coastal waters of Canada (src:6673)
GIVEN waters IS A `s 339(6) waters`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339(6) the waters are coastal waters of Canada` MEANS
    CONSIDER waters
    WHEN `s 339(6) all of Queen Charlotte Sound` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 339(6) all the Strait of Georgia` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 339(6) the Canadian waters of the Strait of Juan de Fuca` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 339(6) other waters` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "coastal waters of Canada includes" lists three places without closing the list

DECLARE `s 339(6) lumber kind` IS ONE OF
    `s 339(6) timber`
    `s 339(6) a mast`
    `s 339(6) a spar`
    `s 339(6) a shingle bolt`
    `s 339(6) a sawlog`
    `s 339(6) lumber of any description`
    `s 339(6) a thing that is none of those`

-- src:6674 | lumber means timber, mast, spar, shingle bolt, sawlog or lumber of any description; (bois)
@ref Criminal Code s 339(6) lumber (src:6674)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 339(6) lumber kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339(6) the thing is lumber` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 339(6) timber` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 339(6) a mast` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 339(6) a spar` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 339(6) a shingle bolt` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 339(6) a sawlog` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 339(6) lumber of any description` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 339(6) a thing that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "lumber means timber, mast, spar, shingle bolt, sawlog or lumber of any description"

DECLARE `s 339(6) lumbering equipment kind` IS ONE OF
    `s 339(6) a boom chain`
    `s 339(6) a chain`
    `s 339(6) a line`
    `s 339(6) a shackle`
    `s 339(6) another thing`

-- src:6675 | lumbering equipment includes a boom chain, chain, line and shackle. (matériel d’exploitation forestière)
@ref Criminal Code s 339(6) lumbering equipment (src:6675)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 339(6) lumbering equipment kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339(6) the thing is lumbering equipment` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 339(6) a boom chain` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 339(6) a chain` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 339(6) a line` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 339(6) a shackle` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 339(6) another thing` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "lumbering equipment includes" lists four things without closing the list

-- src:6676 | Destroying documents of title
-- src:6677 | 340 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, for a fraudulent purpose, destroys, cancels, conceals or obliterates
-- src:6678 | (a) a document of title to goods or lands,
-- src:6679 | (b) a valuable security or testamentary instrument, or
-- src:6680 | (c) a judicial or official document.
@ref Criminal Code s 340 (src:6676-6680)
GIVEN `the person acted for a fraudulent purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person destroys, cancels, conceals or obliterates the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a document of title to goods, by s 2 document of title to goods` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a document of title to lands, by s 2 document of title to lands` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a valuable security, by s 2 valuable security` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a testamentary instrument, by s 2 testamentary instrument` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a judicial or official document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 340 the person commits the offence of destroying documents of title` MEANS
    IF `the person acted for a fraudulent purpose` AND `the person destroys, cancels, conceals or obliterates the thing`
    THEN `ccc12 or` (`ccc12 or` (`ccc12 or` `the thing is a document of title to goods, by s 2 document of title to goods` `the thing is a document of title to lands, by s 2 document of title to lands`)
                                (`ccc12 or` `the thing is a valuable security, by s 2 valuable security` `the thing is a testamentary instrument, by s 2 testamentary instrument`))
                    (JUST `the thing is a judicial or official document`)
         -- JUST FALSE where every kind of thing is a definite no; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where an s 2 answer was not given and no other kind holds
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who, for a fraudulent purpose, destroys, cancels, conceals or obliterates"

@ref Criminal Code s 340 (src:6677-6677)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 340 the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:6681 | Fraudulent concealment
-- src:6682 | 341 Every person who, for a fraudulent purpose, takes, obtains, removes or conceals anything is guilty of
-- src:6683 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:6684 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 341 (src:6681-6684)
GIVEN `the person acted for a fraudulent purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person takes, obtains, removes or conceals anything` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 341 the person commits the offence of fraudulent concealment` MEANS
    IF `the person acted for a fraudulent purpose` AND `the person takes, obtains, removes or conceals anything`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who, for a fraudulent purpose, takes, obtains, removes or conceals anything"

@ref Criminal Code s 341 (src:6683-6684)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 341 the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`)   -- (a) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than two years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction

§§ `Sections 342 to 342.2 -- credit cards, credit card data, computers`

-- src:6685 | Theft, forgery, etc., of credit card
-- src:6686 | 342 (1) Every person who
-- src:6687 | (a) steals a credit card,
-- src:6688 | (b) forges or falsifies a credit card,
-- src:6689 | (c) possesses, uses or traffics in a credit card or a forged or falsified credit card, knowing that it was obtained, made or altered
-- src:6690 | (i) by the commission in Canada of an offence, or
-- src:6691 | (ii) by an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence, or
-- src:6692 | (d) uses a credit card knowing that it has been revoked or cancelled,
-- src:6693 | is guilty of
-- src:6694 | (e) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years, or
-- src:6695 | (f) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 342(1) (src:6685-6695)
GIVEN `the thing is a credit card, by s 321 the thing is a credit card` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person steals the credit card, by s 2 steal` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person forges or falsifies a credit card` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses, uses or traffics in a credit card or a forged or falsified credit card` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that it was obtained, made or altered by the commission in Canada of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that it was obtained, made or altered by an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses a credit card knowing that it has been revoked or cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342(1) the person commits the offence of theft, forgery, etc., of a credit card` MEANS
    `ccc12 and` `the thing is a credit card, by s 321 the thing is a credit card`
                (`ccc12 or` `the person steals the credit card, by s 2 steal` (JUST (`para (b)` OR `para (c)` OR `para (d)`)))
    -- JUST FALSE where the thing is a definite no or no paragraph holds: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who (a) steals a credit card, (b) forges or falsifies a credit card, (c) possesses, uses or traffics in a credit card or a forged or falsified credit card, knowing that it was obtained, made or altered"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 321 or s 2 "steal" answer was not given and nothing else settles it
    WHERE
        `para (b)` MEANS `the person forges or falsifies a credit card`
        `para (c)` MEANS
                `the person possesses, uses or traffics in a credit card or a forged or falsified credit card`
            AND (   `the person knows that it was obtained, made or altered by the commission in Canada of an offence`
                 OR `the person knows that it was obtained, made or altered by an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence`)
        `para (d)` MEANS `the person uses a credit card knowing that it has been revoked or cancelled`

@ref Criminal Code s 342(1) (src:6693-6695)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 342(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (e) an indictable offence, imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (f) an offence punishable on summary conviction

DECLARE `s 342(2) place` IS ONE OF
    `s 342(2) the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed`
    `s 342(2) the place where the accused is found`
    `s 342(2) the place where the accused is arrested`
    `s 342(2) the place where the accused is in custody`
    `s 342(2) another place`

-- src:6696 | Jurisdiction
-- src:6697 | (2) An accused who is charged with an offence under subsection (1) may be tried and punished by any court having jurisdiction to try that offence in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed or in the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody, but where the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody is outside the province in which the offence is alleged to have been committed, no proceedings in respect of that offence shall be commenced in that place without the consent of the Attorney General of that province.
@ref Criminal Code s 342(2) (src:6696-6697)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with an offence under subsection 342(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A `s 342(2) place`
      `the court has jurisdiction to try that offence in that place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342(2) the accused may be tried and punished by the court in the place` MEANS
    IF `the accused is charged with an offence under subsection 342(1)` AND `the court has jurisdiction to try that offence in that place`
    THEN CONSIDER place
         WHEN `s 342(2) the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 342(2) the place where the accused is found` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 342(2) the place where the accused is arrested` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 342(2) the place where the accused is in custody` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 342(2) another place` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names four places; it grants nothing for another
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("may be tried and punished") for an accused charged under (1) before a court that has jurisdiction in the place

GIVEN `the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody is outside the province in which the offence is alleged to have been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of that province has consented to the commencement of the proceedings in that place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342(2) proceedings in the place may not be commenced without the consent of the Attorney General of the province` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody is outside the province in which the offence is alleged to have been committed`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but where the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody is outside the province in which the offence is alleged to have been committed" (a "where" gate unmet: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF `the Attorney General of that province has consented to the commencement of the proceedings in that place`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is "without the consent of the Attorney General of that province"; with the consent the subsection says nothing more
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:6698 | Unauthorized use of credit card data
-- src:6699 | (3) Every person who, fraudulently and without colour of right, possesses, uses, traffics in or permits another person to use credit card data, including personal authentication information, whether or not the data is authentic, that would enable a person to use a credit card or to obtain the services that are provided by the issuer of a credit card to credit card holders is guilty of
-- src:6700 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years; or
-- src:6701 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 342(3) (src:6698-6701)
GIVEN `the person acted fraudulently and without colour of right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses, uses, traffics in or permits another person to use credit card data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data would enable a person to use a credit card or to obtain the services that are provided by the issuer of a credit card to credit card holders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342(3) the person commits the offence of unauthorized use of credit card data` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted fraudulently and without colour of right`
      AND `the person possesses, uses, traffics in or permits another person to use credit card data`
      AND `the data would enable a person to use a credit card or to obtain the services that are provided by the issuer of a credit card to credit card holders`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who, fraudulently and without colour of right, possesses, uses, traffics in or permits another person to use credit card data"

@ref Criminal Code s 342(3) (src:6699-6701)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 342(3) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (a) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction

-- src:6704 | personal authentication information means a personal identification number or any other password or information that a credit card holder creates or adopts to be used to authenticate his or her identity in relation to the credit card; (authentifiant personnel)
@ref Criminal Code s 342(4) personal authentication information (src:6704)
GIVEN `it is a personal identification number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is any other password or information that a credit card holder creates or adopts to be used to authenticate his or her identity in relation to the credit card` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342(4) the information is personal authentication information` MEANS
    IF `it is a personal identification number` OR `it is any other password or information that a credit card holder creates or adopts to be used to authenticate his or her identity in relation to the credit card`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "personal authentication information means a personal identification number or any other password or information that a credit card holder creates or adopts"

-- src:6705 | traffic means, in relation to a credit card or credit card data, to sell, export from or import into Canada, distribute or deal with in any other way. (trafic)
@ref Criminal Code s 342(4) traffic (src:6705)
GIVEN `the person sells, exports from or imports into Canada, distributes or deals with in any other way the credit card or credit card data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342(4) the person traffics in the credit card or credit card data` MEANS
    IF `the person sells, exports from or imports into Canada, distributes or deals with in any other way the credit card or credit card data`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "traffic means, in relation to a credit card or credit card data, to sell, export from or import into Canada, distribute or deal with in any other way"

-- src:6706 | Instruments for copying credit card data or forging or falsifying credit cards
-- src:6707 | 342.01 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years, or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction, who, without lawful justification or excuse, makes, repairs, buys, sells, exports from Canada, imports into Canada or possesses any instrument, device, apparatus, material or thing that they know has been used or know is adapted or intended for use
-- src:6708 | (a) in the copying of credit card data for use in the commission of an offence under subsection 342(3); or
-- src:6709 | (b) in the forging or falsifying of credit cards.
@ref Criminal Code s 342.01(1) (src:6706-6709)
GIVEN `the person acted without lawful justification or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes, repairs, buys, sells, exports from Canada, imports into Canada or possesses the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the thing has been used, or knows that it is adapted or intended for use, in the copying of credit card data for use in the commission of an offence under subsection 342(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the thing has been used, or knows that it is adapted or intended for use, in the forging or falsifying of credit cards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.01(1) the person commits the offence of possessing instruments for copying credit card data or forging or falsifying credit cards` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted without lawful justification or excuse`
      AND `the person makes, repairs, buys, sells, exports from Canada, imports into Canada or possesses the thing`
      AND (   `the person knows that the thing has been used, or knows that it is adapted or intended for use, in the copying of credit card data for use in the commission of an offence under subsection 342(3)`
           OR `the person knows that the thing has been used, or knows that it is adapted or intended for use, in the forging or falsifying of credit cards`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence ... who, without lawful justification or excuse, makes, repairs, buys, sells, exports from Canada, imports into Canada or possesses any instrument, device, apparatus, material or thing that they know has been used or know is adapted or intended for use"

@ref Criminal Code s 342.01(1) (src:6707-6707)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 342.01(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:6710 | Forfeiture
-- src:6711 | (2) Where a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1), any instrument, device, apparatus, material or thing in relation to which the offence was committed or the possession of which constituted the offence may, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed, be ordered forfeited to Her Majesty, whereupon it may be disposed of as the Attorney General directs.
@ref Criminal Code s 342.01(2) (src:6710-6711)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection 342.01(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is one in relation to which the offence was committed, or the possession of which constituted the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.01(2) the thing may be ordered forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection 342.01(1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1), any instrument, device, apparatus, material or thing in relation to which the offence was committed or the possession of which constituted the offence may, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed, be ordered forfeited to Her Majesty" (a failed "where" gate, by ruling (b) of 2026-11-05; but this function is named for a power ("may"), so it is one of the "may" functions gated by "where" that the fork register lists for a lawyer: fork F-MAY-WHERE)
    ELSE IF `the thing is one in relation to which the offence was committed, or the possession of which constituted the offence`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power covers "any instrument, device, apparatus, material or thing in relation to which the offence was committed or the possession of which constituted the offence"; for another thing the subsection grants nothing and denies nothing

-- src:6712 | Limitation
-- src:6713 | (3) No order of forfeiture may be made under subsection (2) in respect of any thing that is the property of a person who was not a party to the offence under subsection (1).
@ref Criminal Code s 342.01(3) (src:6712-6713)
GIVEN `the thing is the property of a person who was not a party to the offence under subsection 342.01(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.01(3) an order of forfeiture is barred` MEANS
    IF `the thing is the property of a person who was not a party to the offence under subsection 342.01(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No order of forfeiture may be made under subsection (2) in respect of any thing that is the property of a person who was not a party to the offence under subsection (1)" (a bar whose gate is unmet)

-- src:6714 | Unauthorized use of computer
-- src:6715 | 342.1 (1) Everyone is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years, or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, fraudulently and without colour of right,
-- src:6716 | (a) obtains, directly or indirectly, any computer service;
-- src:6717 | (b) by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, intercepts or causes to be intercepted, directly or indirectly, any function of a computer system;
-- src:6718 | (c) uses or causes to be used, directly or indirectly, a computer system with intent to commit an offence under paragraph (a) or (b) or under section 430 in relation to computer data or a computer system; or
-- src:6719 | (d) uses, possesses, traffics in or permits another person to have access to a computer password that would enable a person to commit an offence under paragraph (a), (b) or (c).
@ref Criminal Code s 342.1(1) (src:6714-6719)
GIVEN `the person acted fraudulently and without colour of right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person obtains, directly or indirectly, any computer service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, intercepts or causes to be intercepted, directly or indirectly, any function of a computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses or causes to be used, directly or indirectly, a computer system with intent to commit an offence under paragraph (a) or (b) or under section 430 in relation to computer data or a computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses, possesses, traffics in or permits another person to have access to a computer password that would enable a person to commit an offence under paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.1(1) the person commits the offence of unauthorized use of a computer` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted fraudulently and without colour of right`
      AND (   `the person obtains, directly or indirectly, any computer service`
           OR `the person, by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, intercepts or causes to be intercepted, directly or indirectly, any function of a computer system`
           OR `the person uses or causes to be used, directly or indirectly, a computer system with intent to commit an offence under paragraph (a) or (b) or under section 430 in relation to computer data or a computer system`
           OR `the person uses, possesses, traffics in or permits another person to have access to a computer password that would enable a person to commit an offence under paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone is guilty of an indictable offence ... who, fraudulently and without colour of right"

@ref Criminal Code s 342.1(1) (src:6715-6715)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 342.1(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- Subsection (2): the definitions "In this section". "means" closes a definition (JUST FALSE outside it); "includes" does not (NOTHING outside the named cases).
-- src:6722 | computer data means representations, including signs, signals or symbols, that are in a form suitable for processing in a computer system; (données informatiques)
@ref Criminal Code s 342.1(2) computer data (src:6722)
GIVEN `it is representations, including signs, signals or symbols` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in a form suitable for processing in a computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.1(2) computer data` MEANS
    IF `it is representations, including signs, signals or symbols` AND `it is in a form suitable for processing in a computer system`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "computer data means representations, including signs, signals or symbols, that are in a form suitable for processing in a computer system"

-- src:6723 | computer password means any computer data by which a computer service or computer system is capable of being obtained or used; (mot de passe)
@ref Criminal Code s 342.1(2) computer password (src:6723)
GIVEN `it is computer data, by s 342.1(2) computer data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `by it a computer service or computer system is capable of being obtained or used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.1(2) computer password` MEANS
    IF `by it a computer service or computer system is capable of being obtained or used`
    THEN `it is computer data, by s 342.1(2) computer data`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE if it is definitely not computer data; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where that answer was not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "computer password means any computer data by which a computer service or computer system is capable of being obtained or used"

-- src:6724 | computer program means computer data representing instructions or statements that, when executed in a computer system, causes the computer system to perform a function; (programme d’ordinateur)
@ref Criminal Code s 342.1(2) computer program (src:6724)
GIVEN `it is computer data, by s 342.1(2) computer data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it represents instructions or statements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `when executed in a computer system it causes the computer system to perform a function` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.1(2) computer program` MEANS
    IF `it represents instructions or statements` AND `when executed in a computer system it causes the computer system to perform a function`
    THEN `it is computer data, by s 342.1(2) computer data`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE if it is definitely not computer data; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where that answer was not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "computer program means computer data representing instructions or statements that, when executed in a computer system, causes the computer system to perform a function"

DECLARE `s 342.1(2) computer service kind` IS ONE OF
    `s 342.1(2) data processing`
    `s 342.1(2) the storage of computer data`
    `s 342.1(2) the retrieval of computer data`
    `s 342.1(2) another service`

-- src:6725 | computer service includes data processing and the storage or retrieval of computer data; (service d’ordinateur)
@ref Criminal Code s 342.1(2) computer service (src:6725)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 342.1(2) computer service kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.1(2) computer service` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) data processing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) the storage of computer data` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) the retrieval of computer data` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) another service` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "computer service includes data processing and the storage or retrieval of computer data"

-- src:6726 | computer system means a device that, or a group of interconnected or related devices one or more of which,
-- src:6727 | (a) contains computer programs or other computer data, and
-- src:6728 | (b) by means of computer programs,
-- src:6729 | (i) performs logic and control, and
-- src:6730 | (ii) may perform any other function; (ordinateur)
@ref Criminal Code s 342.1(2) computer system (src:6726-6730)
GIVEN `it is a device, or a group of interconnected or related devices one or more of which` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contains computer programs or other computer data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by means of computer programs it performs logic and control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by means of computer programs it may perform any other function` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.1(2) computer system` MEANS
    IF    `it is a device, or a group of interconnected or related devices one or more of which`
      AND `it contains computer programs or other computer data`
      AND `by means of computer programs it performs logic and control`
      AND `by means of computer programs it may perform any other function`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "computer system means a device that, or a group of interconnected or related devices one or more of which, (a) contains computer programs or other computer data, and (b) by means of computer programs, (i) performs logic and control, and (ii) may perform any other function"

-- src:6731 | data [Repealed, 2014, c. 31, s. 16]
@ref Criminal Code s 342.1(2) data (src:6731)
`s 342.1(2) data as the text shows it` MEANS "data [Repealed, 2014, c. 31, s. 16]"

-- src:6732 | electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device means any device or apparatus that is used or is capable of being used to intercept any function of a computer system, but does not include a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing; (dispositif électromagnétique, acoustique, mécanique ou autre)
@ref Criminal Code s 342.1(2) electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device (src:6732)
GIVEN `it is a device or apparatus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used or is capable of being used to intercept any function of a computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.1(2) electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing"
        IF `it is a device or apparatus` AND `it is used or is capable of being used to intercept any function of a computer system`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any device or apparatus that is used or is capable of being used to intercept any function of a computer system"

DECLARE `s 342.1(2) function kind` IS ONE OF
    `s 342.1(2) logic`
    `s 342.1(2) control`
    `s 342.1(2) arithmetic`
    `s 342.1(2) deletion`
    `s 342.1(2) storage and retrieval`
    `s 342.1(2) communication or telecommunication to, from or within a computer system`
    `s 342.1(2) another function`

-- src:6733 | function includes logic, control, arithmetic, deletion, storage and retrieval and communication or telecommunication to, from or within a computer system; (fonction)
@ref Criminal Code s 342.1(2) function (src:6733)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 342.1(2) function kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.1(2) function` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) logic` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) control` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) arithmetic` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) deletion` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) storage and retrieval` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) communication or telecommunication to, from or within a computer system` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) another function` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "function includes" lists six cases without closing the list

DECLARE `s 342.1(2) intercept kind` IS ONE OF
    `s 342.1(2) to listen to a function of a computer system`
    `s 342.1(2) to record a function of a computer system`
    `s 342.1(2) to acquire the substance, meaning or purport of a function of a computer system`
    `s 342.1(2) another act`

-- src:6734 | intercept includes listen to or record a function of a computer system, or acquire the substance, meaning or purport thereof; (intercepter)
@ref Criminal Code s 342.1(2) intercept (src:6734)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 342.1(2) intercept kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.1(2) intercept` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) to listen to a function of a computer system` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) to record a function of a computer system` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) to acquire the substance, meaning or purport of a function of a computer system` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 342.1(2) another act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "intercept includes listen to or record a function of a computer system, or acquire the substance, meaning or purport thereof"

-- src:6735 | traffic means, in respect of a computer password, to sell, export from or import into Canada, distribute or deal with in any other way. (trafic)
@ref Criminal Code s 342.1(2) traffic (src:6735)
GIVEN `the person sells, exports from or imports into Canada, distributes or deals with in any other way the computer password` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.1(2) the person traffics in the computer password` MEANS
    IF `the person sells, exports from or imports into Canada, distributes or deals with in any other way the computer password`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "traffic means, in respect of a computer password, to sell, export from or import into Canada, distribute or deal with in any other way"

-- src:6736 | Possession of device to obtain unauthorized use of computer system or to commit mischief
-- src:6737 | 342.2 (1) Every person who, without lawful excuse, makes, possesses, sells, offers for sale, imports, obtains for use, distributes or makes available a device that is designed or adapted primarily to commit an offence under section 342.1 or 430, knowing that the device has been used or is intended to be used to commit such an offence, is
-- src:6738 | (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:6739 | (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 342.2(1) (src:6736-6739)
GIVEN `the person acted without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes, possesses, sells, offers for sale, imports, obtains for use, distributes or makes available the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a device, by s 342.2(4) the thing is a device` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the device is designed or adapted primarily to commit an offence under section 342.1 or 430` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the device has been used or is intended to be used to commit such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.2(1) the person commits the offence of possessing a device to obtain unauthorized use of a computer system or to commit mischief` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted without lawful excuse`
      AND `the person makes, possesses, sells, offers for sale, imports, obtains for use, distributes or makes available the thing`
      AND `the device is designed or adapted primarily to commit an offence under section 342.1 or 430`
      AND `the person knows that the device has been used or is intended to be used to commit such an offence`
    THEN `the thing is a device, by s 342.2(4) the thing is a device`   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): where the answer of subsection (4), "device includes", was not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who, without lawful excuse, makes, possesses, sells, offers for sale, imports, obtains for use, distributes or makes available a device that is designed or adapted primarily to commit an offence under section 342.1 or 430"

@ref Criminal Code s 342.2(1) (src:6738-6739)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 342.2(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`)   -- (a) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than two years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction

-- src:6740 | Forfeiture
-- src:6741 | (2) If a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1), in addition to any punishment that is imposed, any device in relation to which the offence was committed or the possession of which constituted the offence may be ordered forfeited to Her Majesty and may be disposed of as the Attorney General directs.
@ref Criminal Code s 342.2(2) (src:6740-6741)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection 342.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the device is one in relation to which the offence was committed, or the possession of which constituted the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.2(2) the device may be ordered forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection 342.2(1)` AND `the device is one in relation to which the offence was committed, or the possession of which constituted the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("may be ordered forfeited") for a conviction under (1) and a device connected with the offence

-- src:6742 | Limitation
-- src:6743 | (3) No order of forfeiture may be made under subsection (2) in respect of any thing that is the property of a person who was not a party to the offence under subsection (1).
@ref Criminal Code s 342.2(3) (src:6742-6743)
GIVEN `the thing is the property of a person who was not a party to the offence under subsection 342.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.2(3) an order of forfeiture is barred` MEANS
    IF `the thing is the property of a person who was not a party to the offence under subsection 342.2(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No order of forfeiture may be made under subsection (2) in respect of any thing that is the property of a person who was not a party to the offence under subsection (1)" (a bar whose gate is unmet)

-- src:6744 | Definition of device
-- src:6745 | (4) In this section, device includes
-- src:6746 | (a) a component of a device; and
-- src:6747 | (b) a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2).
@ref Criminal Code s 342.2(4) (src:6744-6747)
GIVEN `it is a component of a device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2), by s 342.1(2) computer program` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342.2(4) the thing is a device` MEANS
    IF `it is a component of a device`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `it is a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2), by s 342.1(2) computer program`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "device includes" lists without closing the list
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of subsection 342.1(2) was not given
